# THE CAPTURE CENSUS, AS A GATE - part 24 Phase 59 slice 1b.
#
# CTJSOps.td and BytecodeImport.cpp state that 219 of bootstrap's 1,023 capture
# operands are the importer's `undefined` placeholder carrying an
# `enclosing_indices` entry (1,021 until the ctjs parser of 2026-09-12 read two
# more; the 219 did not move). tools/check/capture-census.py counts both over
# the module the importer actually writes; --expect-indexed is a floor AND a
# ceiling, so a change that stops writing the attribute and one that starts
# writing it where a real binding sits are both caught. It measures the
# IMPORTER ONLY - one pass, no lowering, and no --mlir-print-debuginfo, since
# the census counts operands and attributes and the location suffixes would
# only lengthen a textual parse.
#
# RUN: ctjs-translate --ctbrowser-js-to-ctjs %{monorepo}/ctbrowser/vendor/bootstrap/bootstrap.bundle.js -o %t.mlir
# RUN: python3 %{monorepo}/tools/check/capture-census.py --expect-indexed 219 --expect-operands 1023 %t.mlir
